# requirements/relativity/einstein-1921.ears
capability: Einstein 1921 globular-cluster rerun
owner: relativity
requirements:
  - id: REL-011
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The relativity module shall report Einstein's 1921 equation (5) as printed, as recomputed with his coefficient, and with the factor 3 pi / 32 that his density law gives, each in cm and light-years."
    rationale: "Einstein printed A of about 0.6 for his eq. (3); the Plummer value is 3 pi / 32, about 0.295, so his radius is about twice what his own model gives. The paper's numbers are set beside the recomputed ones, never replaced (docs/protocols/uc03-einstein-1921.md, part A)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_einstein1921::test_the_factor_for_einsteins_density_law_is_three_pi_over_32_not_six_tenths"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_einstein1921::test_part_a_sets_the_printed_numbers_beside_the_recomputed_and_corrected_ones"
  - id: REL-012
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The relativity module shall derive the cluster mass from the isotropic Plummer relations sigma_0^2 = (3 pi / 64) G M / a and <v^2> = (3 pi / 32) G M / a, checked against the Jeans equation."
    rationale: "The mass rests on these relations; a slip in one is the same kind of error the 1921 paper made."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_einstein1921::test_the_projected_dispersion_follows_from_the_jeans_equation"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_einstein1921::test_the_mean_square_speed_is_the_virial_one_and_inverts_to_the_mass"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_einstein1921::test_the_annulus_holds_the_plummer_share_of_the_stars"
  - id: REL-013
    pattern: event
    text: "When the relativity module fits a Gaia cone for UC-03, the relativity module shall fit Einstein's density law, the Plummer projected dispersion and one cluster parallax against a field population, with each star's own errors, in the predeclared annulus."
    rationale: "Einstein's inputs were guesses; Gaia measures the motions, the scale and the distance. Validated on synthetic Plummer clusters with a planted mass and mass-to-light ratio."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_einstein1921::test_the_fit_recovers_the_planted_mass_distance_and_light"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_einstein1921::test_a_heavy_planted_cluster_is_found_heavy"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_einstein1921::test_too_few_stars_in_the_annulus_is_refused_by_name"
  - id: REL-014
    pattern: unwanted
    text: "If a UC-03 scenario or bootstrap refit fails or the baseline band and every scenario do not fall on one side of the predeclared mass-to-light threshold, then the relativity module shall not report a verdict other than inconclusive."
    rationale: "The decision rule is fixed before the data; a split across scenarios is reported, never resolved by choosing a scenario."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_einstein1921::test_the_verdict_supports_einstein_only_when_the_band_and_every_scenario_are_below_ten"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_einstein1921::test_the_verdict_goes_against_einstein_only_when_everything_is_at_or_above_ten"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_einstein1921::test_a_failed_scenario_or_a_missing_bootstrap_makes_the_verdict_inconclusive"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_einstein1921::test_a_bootstrap_with_any_failed_refit_decides_nothing"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_einstein1921::test_a_refit_that_raises_is_recorded_as_a_failure_not_an_abort"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_einstein1921::test_the_predeclared_grid_has_48_scenarios_and_contains_the_baseline"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_einstein1921::test_the_verdict_follows_the_planted_mass_to_light_ratio"
  - id: REL-015
    pattern: event
    text: "When the relativity module writes a UC-03 report, the relativity module shall record the SHA-256 of the committed choices, whether the run's choices match them, the bootstrap seed, and the rows each selection cut removed."
    rationale: "The choices were committed before any M13 data was read; a run under different choices must say so."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_einstein1921::test_a_run_records_the_committed_choices_and_says_when_they_were_changed"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_einstein1921::test_selection_counts_the_rows_each_cut_removes_in_order"
  - id: REL-016
    pattern: event
    text: "When a researcher runs sdp einstein1921 run, the command-line interface shall read the predeclared M13 cone from the complete bulk Gaia copy or from a named Parquet file, refuse an incomplete bulk copy, and write the report as JSON and Markdown."
    rationale: "Leigh's bulk copy is the data; a Parquet cone lets the same run happen without it."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.cli.test_cli_einstein1921::test_a_run_reads_the_predeclared_cone_from_the_bulk_copy_and_writes_both_reports"
      - "python/tests.cli.test_cli_einstein1921::test_a_run_from_parquet_matches_the_bulk_copy"
      - "python/tests.cli.test_cli_einstein1921::test_an_incomplete_bulk_copy_is_refused"
  - id: REL-017
    pattern: event
    text: "When the relativity module runs the UC-03b corrections, the relativity module shall convert UC-03's fit at the published M13 distance and set the mass against the published total V light scaled to that distance, each value read from the committed choices file with its source."
    rationale: "The first UC-03 run was inconclusive, and its spread followed the parallax zero-point and the missing faint light. A published distance and a whole-cluster light remove both, at the cost of depending on that published work (docs/protocols/uc03b-einstein-1921-corrections.md)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_einstein1921_corrections::test_the_distances_are_the_published_ones_from_the_choices_file"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_einstein1921_corrections::test_the_published_light_is_mass_over_mass_to_light_scaled_as_distance_squared"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_einstein1921_corrections::test_a_biased_parallax_no_longer_sets_the_mass"
  - id: REL-018
    pattern: event
    text: "When the relativity module reads the UC-03b corrections, the relativity module shall label the reading exploratory, mark a fit whose scale is below 0.2 of the core cut as degenerate and leave it out, call the reading consistent with H1 or H0 only when the corrected baseline band and every counted correction lie on that side of the threshold with a complete bootstrap, and report the crowding table and the published comparison values."
    rationale: "The corrections were chosen after seeing a result, so they explain UC-03's verdict and never replace it."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_einstein1921_corrections::test_the_grid_has_108_corrections_and_contains_the_baseline"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_einstein1921_corrections::test_the_reading_needs_the_band_and_every_correction_on_one_side"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_einstein1921_corrections::test_the_reading_follows_the_planted_ratio_whatever_the_parallax"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_einstein1921_corrections::test_a_run_records_its_choices_the_crowding_table_and_the_comparisons"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_einstein1921_corrections::test_a_magnitude_limit_fainter_than_uc03s_selection_is_refused"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_einstein1921_corrections::test_a_scale_far_inside_the_core_cut_is_degenerate"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_einstein1921_corrections::test_degenerate_corrections_are_listed_and_left_out_of_the_reading"
  - id: REL-019
    pattern: event
    text: "When a researcher runs sdp einstein1921 corrections, the command-line interface shall read the same M13 cone as sdp einstein1921 run and write the exploratory report as JSON and Markdown beside the UC-03 report."
    rationale: "Leigh reruns on the bulk copy; the Markdown says the reading is exploratory and that UC-03's verdict is unchanged."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.cli.test_cli_einstein1921::test_the_corrections_command_writes_an_exploratory_report_beside_uc03s"
  - id: REL-020
    pattern: event
    text: "When a researcher runs sdp einstein1921 export, the command-line interface shall write the M13 stars that pass UC-03's cuts, with the columns UC-03 reads, to one Parquet file."
    rationale: "The file is the recorded data for the M13 known-answer test: small enough to commit, and it reruns to the same baseline as the whole cone."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.cli.test_cli_einstein1921::test_export_writes_the_stars_that_pass_the_cuts_and_they_rerun_alike"
  - id: REL-021
    pattern: event
    text: "When the relativity test suite runs on the recorded M13 cone, the relativity module shall reproduce UC-03's inconclusive split about the threshold, recover the bright-star mass within 20% of the published mass, keep the corrected V-band mass-to-light ratio below 10, and flag the 6 arcmin core cut as degenerate."
    rationale: "M13 is the known-answer case: real Gaia stars and an independently published mass (Baumgardt database). It guards the fit, the selection and the corrections against regressions on real data, not only synthetic clusters."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T8]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_m13_recorded::test_the_recorded_cone_is_the_one_committed_and_every_star_passes_the_cuts"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_m13_recorded::test_uc03_on_m13_straddles_the_threshold_so_its_verdict_is_inconclusive"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_m13_recorded::test_the_bright_stars_recover_the_published_mass_of_m13"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_m13_recorded::test_with_published_distance_and_light_m13_bears_out_einsteins_conclusion"
      - "python/tests.relativity.test_m13_recorded::test_a_six_arcminute_core_cut_on_m13_is_flagged_degenerate"
